  "prefLabel": "Nat 301.07 Naturopathic Physicians Licensing Examinations (NPLEX)",
  "priorExpiration": "2013-06-18",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nat 301.07 “Naturopathic Physicians Licensing Examinations (NPLEX)” means the examinations administered by NABNE consisting of part I covering basic sciences and part II covering clinical sciences and designed to establish minimum uniform national standards of competence for naturopathic license applicants.\n\nSource. #6380, eff 11-26-96, EXPIRED: 11-26-04\n\nNew. #8374, eff 6-18-05, EXPIRED: 6-18-13\n\nNew. #12176, eff 5-17-17",
